grab some delicious peach pie and stay  off my property  off my property  because we finally have a jack reacher  that's over five foot seven amazon's  reacher is a throwback to when men  didn't cry and action dialogue was just  that perfect level of cheesy i will ruin  your life with one phone call i'll end  your life with one phone  so reach for that like and subscribe  button yes the puns get worse as we take  a deep dive into the ending of reacher i  don't give a [ __ ] meet jack reacher a  six foot five ex-army major who loves  the blues almost as much as he loves  kicking ass  he's found himself in margrave georgia  to visit the site where one of his  favorite jazz musicians blind blake died  in fact if you listen carefully this  song that plays in the very last scene  of the season is blind blake's police  dog blues which has the line all my life  i've been a traveling man which  perfectly encapsulates reacher's  character reacher believes the world is  composed of two types of people people  who stay in one place and people who  wander he believes he's a wanderer that  it's just part of his nature this is  also why he makes sure to correct people  when they call him a vagrant  for the record i'm not a vagrant i'm a  hobo vagrants are people with no jobs  while hobos have historically been  migratory laborers and reacher isn't one  to stray away from work especially if it  means taking down the bad guys this  compulsion to constantly move is so  strong that he leaves behind love  interest roscoe conklin at the end of  the season but if he's such a wanderer  what makes him stay in margrave at the  end of the first episode reacher finds  out that his brother joe just happened  to be murdered in the same town the  night before prompting him to take on a  sort of vigilante justice i'm batman  what he uncovers is an international  criminal organization with crooked cops  spanning local state and federal levels  an organization his brother was looking  to take down but got him killed in the  process teaming up with margrave  detective finlay and officer roscoe  conklin reacher finds out that mayor  teal and beloved multi-millionaire  businessman kleiner have been working  with a criminal organization in  venezuela to produce millions in  counterfeit bills throughout the season  reacher learns that his brother who was  working in the anti-counterfeiting  department of the secret service was  close to uncovering this scheme the only  thing he didn't have was concrete proof  linking those involved with those  counterfeit bills so reacher takes it  upon himself to avenge his brother and  put these bad guys away i guess i'll  find everybody responsible  and kill every last one of them and this  motivation to do what is right stems  from his childhood throughout the season  we get flashbacks of reacher and his  brother as kids reacher beats up a bully  and when he's forced to apologize he  doesn't go through with it even though  it could cost his father his job his  mother sees this strength in him wanting  him to harness it for good you have the  strength of three boys your age  what will you do with that strength  you're going to do what's right perhaps  this was part of his motivation to join  the military not only would it be  following in the footsteps of his father  but it would allow him to do good while  remaining congruent with his wandering  spirit but let's get into the real meat  and potatoes of what's going on in  margrave this is kleiner senior and he  runs a big company that does everything  from manufacturing air conditioners  chemicals and all sorts of random things  he's found a way to counterfeit u.s  hundred dollar bills a bill that should  be nearly impossible to counterfeit  because there's only one entity in the  world that has the ability to print the  special type of paper the bills are made  on that's the us mint rather than create  this paper on their own why not bleach  the ink off a standard one dollar bill  then reprint it as a hundred dollar bill  it's a pretty ingenious scheme but  requires a vast amount of poisonous  chemicals to work and those poisonous  chemicals need to be disposed of so  clarin chemical a subsidiary of kleiner  industries has the brilliant plan of  dumping this waste into a river which  alerts an epa agent fearing their scheme  in jeopardy they have this epa agent  killed and the hitmen responsible for  this is a former partner of fbi h and  picard who is friends with detective  finlay picard who's been helping reach  her in the team throughout the season is  actually one of the bad guys what kind  of cop are you the kind that goes where  the money is so kleiner can't keep  spilling toxic waste into the river or  else they might get caught again so what  do they do buy a [ __ ] ton of cow feed of  course cow feed contains something  called a diatomaceous earth which when  ground up can be used as an effective  cleaning agent for chemical waste this  is why kleiner bought a bunch of cows to  cover up the fact he's been buying so  much cow feed which contains that  special compound but reacher still needs  hard evidence to link kleiner with those  counterfeit bills all he has up to this  point are theories this is where paul  hubble comes in he was blackmailed into  becoming kleiner's financial accountant  responsible for laundering money and  acquiring vast amount of one dollar  bills from payday loan shops and casinos  that could be turned into those  counterfeit hundreds he saw firsthand if  he didn't follow what kleiner said he  and his family could be brutally  murdered while doing the books hubble  finds out that someone has been skimming  money from the top which he pinpoints to  a truck driver responsible for  delivering those counterfeit bills named  pete jobling we never really see pete in  the show but hubble knowing if kleiner  found out pete was stealing from him  would have him killed works with pete  and a federal agent to bring kleiner  down in exchange for immunity and who  happens to be that agent reacher's  brother joe unfortunately for joe and  pete they're killed before they can  expose the whole plan a kill scene which  is the very first thing we see in the  show in the second last episode reacher  uncovers pete's stash of counterfeit  cash the stuff he stole from kleiner  which is the evidence they need to link  kleiner to this criminal activity but  kleiner is dead yes his maniacal son  kleiner jr or kj for short killed his  own father to protect the business see  the old man he had the brains to create  this whole operation but he never had  the guts to do what needed to be done to  protect it not only that it was kj who  killed reacher's brother the final  episode becomes a giant showdown at the  kleiner chemical factory the same  factory where this counterfeit money is  produced kj and mayor teal have hubble's  wife and children along with officer  roscoe as hostages making the assault on  this facility by reacher x-comrad neely  finlay and hubble all the more difficult  what i did like about this final action  scene is how every character was given  an antagonist to fight we have finlay  pitted against the man who betrayed him  roscoe and the mayor a man who killed  her father-like figure and reacher vs kj  it's ironic that the chemical used to  take the ink off the dollar bills  becomes the chemical that lights kj on  fire and kills him with the hostages  saved and reacher victorious in the  epilogue we really get to see how our  characters have changed over the course  of the season the biggest change is  arguably with finley a man who couldn't  get over the death of his wife sharon he  moved from boston because everything  there reminded him of her he's a great  foil to reach her whereas reacher lets  go of people too easily finley can't let  go but at the end of the season finley  has found the courage to move on telling  reacher he's ready to move back to  boston and take care of someone else a  dog he adopts and names jack after  reacher's first name roscoe has also  found the strength to take back the town  her family built even joking with  reacher that she may run for mayor but  has reacher changed it's rare in writing  that we have a protagonist who ends a  season of a show the same person than  when they started this is visually  represented with reacher in episode 1  walking by himself on the side of the  road with episode 8 him doing the same  thing if you have such a static  protagonist you have to make sure that  character becomes the catalyst for  change among the others this is why  finlay thanks reacher for his help  saying that he couldn't have moved on  without him and bonus points if you  caught the cameo of jack reacher author  lee child in the diner at the end i  actually thought it was brian cranston  for a moment we get a flashback of  reacher visiting his mother on her  deathbed she gives him a medal of  bravery that belonged to his grandfather  from world war ii richer will end up  burying this medal where his brother  died a symbol of the bravery it took his  brother to do what is right it takes  bravery to do what's right reacher says  goodbye to roscoe richard just isn't a  man to be held down he is a wanderer  after all she gives him a gift of a  clark bar with her phone number on it a  call back to episode 2 where it was one  of the luxurious vending machine options  at their motel and finally we have to  talk about the pie which also happens to  be the title of the final episode  throughout the entire season it's been a  running egg that whenever reacher orders  the peach pie from the diner he gets  called away before he can eat it finally  he gets to enjoy it stating that he's  had better obviously he hasn't had my  grandmas and as we're left with no more  shirtless reacher until potential season  2 i now turn it over to you was reacher  worth the watch or should amazon give it  the boot let me know your thoughts in  the comments below thanks for watching  everyone be sure to like and subscribe  and for more bad takes you can follow me  on twitter and instagram think story yt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much  you

